# .mcpb bundle contents — ALLOWLIST polarity (v0.5.0).
#
# Why allowlist: the previous exclude-list let any NEW root file ship by default
# (.pii-forbidden nearly leaked this way at v0.3.2; pii-guard.config.json did get
# bundled by the old list — caught in the v0.5.0 pack diff). Here we exclude
# EVERYTHING with `/*`, then re-include only the files the runtime needs. A new
# root file is now withheld unless explicitly added below — fail-safe.
#
# `/*` matches top-level entries only (not nested paths), so re-including a
# directory with `!` brings its whole subtree along (verified against the mcpb
# pack engine). Keep node_modules intact: the bundle must ship production deps
# for the server to start.

# Exclude every top-level entry…
/*

# …then re-include only what the runtime needs.
!/build
!/node_modules
!/manifest.json
!/package.json
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
